// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Suspicious Shell Open Command Registry Modification
// Sigma ID: 0d326ee1-b53b-4e20-91c6-d0708cddafd2
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-01-24 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1548.002, T1546.001
// Description: Detects modifications to shell open registry keys that point to suspicious locations typically
//   used by malware for persistence. Generally, modifications to the `*\shell\open\command` registry
//   key can indicate an attempt to change the default action for opening files, and various UAC
//   bypass or persistence techniques involve modifying these keys to execute malicious scripts or
//   binaries.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate software installations or updates that modify the shell open command registry keys to these locations.
// References:
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/25/f/water-curse.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7490edb4783550895f8ac7b1ff297eaa8fda0d2a/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_susp_shell_open_keys_modification_patterns.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\shell\\open\\command.*$" and (RegistryValueData contains "\\$Recycle.Bin\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Contacts\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Music\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\PerfLogs\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Photos\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Pictures\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Users\\Public\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Videos\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Windows\\Temp\\" or RegistryValueData contains "%AppData%" or RegistryValueData contains "%LocalAppData%" or RegistryValueData contains "%Temp%" or RegistryValueData contains "%tmp%")
